MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

It seems sink() works well, e.g. if you only want to record messages:

msg = file('messages.txt', open='wt')
sink(msg, type = 'message')
message('whatever...')

library(knitr)
knit(text = '
<<setup>>=
#hook_msg = function(x, options)
knit_hooks$set(message = function(x, options) {message(x); NULL},
               warning = function(x, options) {warning(x); NULL})
@
<<test>>=
1+1
message("hello...")
warning("howdy!!!")
@
')

warning('I am done now.')
sink(type='message')

Regards,
Yihui
--
